From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter Laux <hunterlaux@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 02:06:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 03/74] MIPS: ingenic: Probe UserLocal instead of assuming it
 is absent

The Ingenic CPU feature overrides were written for the first XBurst
SoCs, whose cores lack the UserLocal register (Config3.ULRI reads as 0
on XBurst1, as its manual says), so they define cpu_has_userlocal as 0.
The XBurst II cores of the X2600 do implement it, but under
that override the kernel never enables it, and every RDHWR $29 from
userspace, the way glibc reads the thread pointer for each access to
thread-local data, traps and is emulated.

Leave it to the Config3 probe, as on other MIPS CPUs. XBurst1 still
reports no UserLocal. On the X2600 a thread pointer read goes from
559 ns to 2.8 ns, returning the same value, with thread-local data
still correct in two threads.
---
 arch/mips/include/asm/mach-ingenic/cpu-feature-overrides.h | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/mips/include/asm/mach-ingenic/cpu-feature-overrides.h b/arch/mips/include/asm/mach-ingenic/cpu-feature-overrides.h
index 7ace50127..08d6e2349 100644
--- a/arch/mips/include/asm/mach-ingenic/cpu-feature-overrides.h
+++ b/arch/mips/include/asm/mach-ingenic/cpu-feature-overrides.h
@@ -37,7 +37,6 @@
 #define cpu_has_dsp		0
 #define cpu_has_dsp2		0
 #define cpu_has_mipsmt		0
-#define cpu_has_userlocal	0
 #define cpu_has_nofpuex 0
 #define cpu_has_64bits		0
 #define cpu_has_64bit_zero_reg 0
